SECTION 3: CLEAN-ROOM RUST 2021 ARCHITECTURE & ZERO EXTERNAL DEPENDENCIES
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
lh-dmverity-builder is engineered from first principles as an independent,
clean-room Rust utility under `#![forbid(unsafe_code)]`.

It operates with 100% zero external crate dependencies ([dependencies] in
Cargo.toml is empty), linking exclusively against the Rust Standard Library (std).
Cryptographic FIPS 180-4 SHA-256 hashing, Merkle tree construction, binary
superblock serialization, and JSON/SARIF parsing are implemented in pure safe Rust.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SECTION 4: TECHNICAL SPECIFICATIONS & STANDARDS CONFORMANCE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
This software conforms to the following standards and specifications:
  - Rust 2021 Edition (ISO/IEC 9899 and safe memory safety guarantees)
  - Linux Kernel Documentation: Documentation/admin-guide/device-mapper/verity.rst
  - NIST FIPS 180-4: Secure Hash Standard (SHA-256)
  - ChromeOS / Android dm-verity v1 On-Disk Superblock Specification
  - OASIS SARIF v2.1.0: Static Analysis Results Interchange Format
  - OWASP & CWE Embedded Security Classifications:
    CWE-353 (Missing Integrity Check / Unprotected Rootfs),
    CWE-693 (Protection Mechanism Failure / Permissive Error Handling),
    CWE-347 (Improper Verification of Cryptographic Signature),
    CWE-328 (Reversible One-Way Hash / Deprecated Algorithm),
    CWE-330 (Use of Insufficiently Random Values / Weak Salt),
    CWE-367 (Time-of-check Time-of-use Race / Missing FEC),
    CWE-400 (Uncontrolled Resource Consumption / Non-4K Blocks),
    CWE-250 (Execution with Unnecessary Privileges / Cmdline Overrides),
    CWE-755 (Improper Handling of Exceptional Conditions / Missing A/B Fallback)
